---
import { codexMarketplace, marketplace } from "@data/navigation";
import { providers } from "@data/providers";
---

<div class="doc-body page-wrap prose">
  <aside class="note"><strong>Upgrading from 2.2 or earlier?</strong><p>Version 2.3 removes the retired CV, GitHub, LinkedIn, portfolio, and X skill modules. Run <code>npx vitaecontext@latest uninstall --provider &lt;provider&gt;</code> before reinstalling so old module folders recorded by the existing install manifest are removed.</p></aside>

  <section>
    <h2>Install from npm</h2>
    <p>Use the provider matching your agent environment:</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>npx vitaecontext install --provider codex</code></pre>
    <p>Replace <code>codex</code> with another published provider value listed below. Source-only adapters require a local checkout.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Supported provider values</h2>
    <div class="simple-table" role="table" aria-label="Supported provider values">
      {providers.map((provider) => <div role="row"><strong role="cell">{provider.id}</strong><span role="cell">{provider.name}{provider.sourceOnly ? " (source only)" : ""}</span><code role="cell">{provider.globalTarget}</code></div>)}
    </div>
    <p><a href="/providers/">See provider-specific commands and invocation examples.</a> For Pi, use the local checkout instructions below until npm support is released.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Model Context Protocol (MCP) Server</h2>
    <p>Connect a compatible agent to selected local Career Context and VitaeGraph files over the stateless Model Context Protocol server:</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>npx -y vitaecontext mcp</code></pre>
    <p><a href="/docs/mcp/">See the full MCP setup guide for Claude Desktop, Cursor, Windsurf, Roo Code, and more.</a></p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Claude Code marketplace</h2>
    <p>Claude Code also supports a plugin marketplace installation:</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>{marketplace.addCommand}
{marketplace.installCommand}</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Codex plugin marketplace</h2>
    <p>A cloned product repository includes a native Codex plugin backed by the same canonical skills:</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>{codexMarketplace.addCommand}
{codexMarketplace.installCommand}</code></pre>
    <p>Direct npm skill installation remains supported and does not require the plugin marketplace.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Local checkout</h2>
    <p>Maintainers can test an unpublished checkout from the product repository:</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>git clone https://github.com/vitaecontext/vitaecontext.git
cd vitaecontext
npx . install --provider codex</code></pre>
    <p>To try the unreleased Pi adapter from the same checkout:</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>node bin/vitaecontext.mjs install --provider pi</code></pre>
    <p>The default destination is <code>~/.pi/agent/skills/</code>; set <code>PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR</code> for a custom Pi directory or pass <code>--project-root .</code> for <code>.pi/skills/</code>. Skill installation does not configure MCP.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Useful install flags</h2>
    <dl class="definition-list">
      <div><dt><code>--project-root &lt;dir&gt;</code></dt><dd>Install relative to a project instead of the global default.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>--target-dir &lt;dir&gt;</code></dt><dd>Use an exact skill destination. Required for the shared provider.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>--commands-target-dir &lt;dir&gt;</code></dt><dd>Override command-wrapper placement where supported.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>--force</code></dt><dd>Replace existing VitaeContext files without prompting.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <aside class="note"><strong>Career files are separate.</strong><p>Installing the package does not collect or upload career material. Provider data rules apply when a person later supplies files to that provider.</p></aside>
</div>
